{% extends "_layouts/default.njk" %}

{% set pageName = "Duplicate record training" %}
{% set headerOptions = {
  service: {
    text: serviceName
  }
} %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

      <!-- Duplicate training demo index -->
      <h1 class="nhsuk-heading-l">Duplicate record training</h1>
      <p class="nhsuk-body">Demo scenarios for reviewing duplicate vaccination records at different set sizes, plus design explorations trying out presentation ideas on top of them.</p>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">Scenarios</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/start">Start page</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Content page introducing the review (placeholder copy), with a CTA into the first record set</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/2-records">2 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Near-identical pair: the same GP event arriving twice from the NHS Immunisations API</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records">3 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Two API echoes plus a sparse historical upload with a divergent date</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/5-records">5 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Mixed API and historical upload set wrapping onto a second row, including a long name that wraps within its card</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records-selected">3 records, selection made</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Pre-selected state: preferred record already chosen, tags and highlighted border from load</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/20-records">20 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Full-scale set: one record made in Mavis among API echoes and historical uploads, with outliers, blank fields and wrapping values</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">From a child record</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/gareth-record">Gareth Greene's MMR record</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">The other way in: a child's MMR vaccination record (as designed on the vaccination-record-valid-ignored-doses branch) whose dose 1 carries a +2 duplicates link. Following it opens the 3-record choosing view without the Review heading, section navigation or queue framing</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">Design explorations</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/2-records-highlighted">2 records, differences highlighted</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Near-identical API pair as in 2 records, with record 2 missing its batch: differences marked with the warm yellow highlight, blanks as a small chip; all the other differences sit behind View all rows. A Highlight differences checkbox in the duplicate summary panel switches the marks on (off by default)</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/6-records-highlighted">6 records, differences highlighted</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Five API echoes and a sparse historical upload, wrapping onto a second row: in any row where values differ, every value is marked with the warm yellow highlight, blanks showing as a small highlighted chip; labels and fully identical rows are unmarked. A Highlight differences checkbox in the duplicate summary panel switches the marks on (off by default)</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/4-records-full">4 records, full record shown</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Three API echoes and a sparse historical upload with every field always on show: no View all rows control, no difference highlighting, and sticky Choose this record footers that ride the viewport within each card on short screens</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records-compact">3 records, compact</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Optimised for sets of 3 or fewer (4 or more are about 0.5% of duplicates): the same 3-record queue scenario at the standard 1100px page width instead of the 1720px canvas, with three record columns, a narrower label column, and tighter gaps and cell padding</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <!-- /Duplicate training demo index -->

    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
